# J-ROC OS — GitHub Repository Setup & Development Roadmap

---

## 🚀 Setting Up the GitHub Repository

### Step 1: Create Repository

```bash
# Create new repository on GitHub
# Name: jroc-os-core
# Description: Autonomous Business Operating System
# Visibility: Public (or Private if commercial)
# Add MIT License
# Add .gitignore for Node.js

# Clone locally
git clone https://github.com/jroc-os/core.git
cd jroc-os
```

### Step 2: Initialize Monorepo

```bash
# Initialize npm monorepo
npm init -w ./apps/api
npm init -w ./apps/web
npm init -w ./packages/agents
npm init -w ./packages/database
npm init -w ./packages/shared
npm init -w ./packages/automation

# Install root dependencies
npm install --save-dev typescript @types/node ts-node

# Install workspace dependencies
npm install -w ./apps/api express pg dotenv anthropic
npm install -w ./apps/web react react-dom redux
npm install -w ./packages/agents axios uuid
```

### Step 3: Setup TypeScript

```bash
# Root tsconfig.json
cat > tsconfig.json << 'EOF'
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "commonjs",
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true
  }
}
EOF
```

### Step 4: Create GitHub Secrets

In GitHub Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions, add:

```
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY        # Claude API key
DATABASE_URL             # PostgreSQL connection string
REDIS_URL                # Redis connection URL
DOCKER_USERNAME          # Docker Hub username
DOCKER_PASSWORD          # Docker Hub password
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID        # AWS credentials (for deployment)
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY    # AWS credentials
GITHUB_TOKEN             # Auto-generated
```

### Step 5: Setup CI/CD Pipeline

```bash
# Create workflows directory
mkdir -p .github/workflows

# Copy workflow files
cp .github/workflows/test.yml .github/workflows/
cp .github/workflows/build.yml .github/workflows/
cp .github/workflows/deploy.yml .github/workflows/
```

### Step 6: Initial Commit & Release

```bash
# Add all files
git add .
git commit -m "chore: initialize j-roc-os monorepo with v4.1.2 structure"

# Create v4.1.2 tag
git tag -a v4.1.2 -m "Release v4.1.2 - Autonomous Revenue Engine"
git push origin main --tags

# Create release notes in GitHub
# Title: J-ROC OS v4.1.2 - Autonomous Revenue Engine
# Include changelog with bug fixes and improvements
```

