## 📋 Versioning Strategy

### Semantic Versioning Rules

```
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-PRERELEASE+BUILD
  4   .  1  .  2    -beta.1      +20240115

MAJOR:  Version number (v1-v12)
MINOR:  Feature release within version
PATCH:  Bug fixes & security updates
```

### Release Types

#### Major Release (v4.0.0 → v5.0.0)
- New primary feature (AI Employees, Automation, etc.)
- Database migrations required
- Breaking API changes possible
- ~4-8 week development cycle
- Requires comprehensive testing

#### Feature Release (v5.1.0)
- New features without breaking changes
- Backward compatible
- Opt-in new functionality
- ~2-4 week development cycle

#### Patch Release (v5.1.1)
- Bug fixes, security updates
- No new features
- ~1 week development cycle

#### Beta/Pre-release (v5.0.0-beta.1)
- Testing phase before major release
- Used for community feedback
- Can have breaking changes

### Release Checklist

```markdown
## Release v5.0.0 - AI Employee System

### Before Release
- [ ] All PRs merged to develop
- [ ] Tests passing (>80% coverage)
- [ ] Database migrations tested
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] Security audit complete
- [ ] Performance benchmarks OK
- [ ] Security secrets rotated

### Release Tasks
- [ ] Create release branch: `release/v5.0.0`
- [ ] Bump version in package.json
- [ ] Update CHANGELOG.md
- [ ] Create GitHub release
- [ ] Build Docker images
- [ ] Tag production deployment
- [ ] Deploy to staging
- [ ] Run smoke tests
- [ ] Deploy to production
- [ ] Monitor for errors

### Post-Release
- [ ] Monitor error rates
- [ ] Check performance metrics
- [ ] Respond to issues
- [ ] Update documentation
- [ ] Create retrospective
```

